<ProjectLayout title="Toast IO — EKS Cost Optimization - Mark Lester Perez" projectTitle="Toast IO — EKS Cost Optimization">
  <h2>Project Overview</h2>
  <p>
    Led a cost optimization initiative for a large-scale EKS environment running 120+ Spring Boot
    microservices. Through data-driven analysis of actual resource consumption, right-sized CPU and
    memory requests/limits across the fleet, achieving 40-60% infrastructure cost savings without
    impacting application performance.
  </p>

  <h2>Technologies Used</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>AWS EKS (Elastic Kubernetes Service)</li>
    <li>Datadog for metrics and monitoring</li>
    <li>Kubernetes HPA (Horizontal Pod Autoscaler)</li>
    <li>Spring Boot microservices</li>
    <li>Helm charts for deployment</li>
    <li>Karpenter for node provisioning</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The Challenge</h2>
  <p>
    The platform ran over 120 Spring Boot microservices on EKS, many of which had been provisioned
    with generous resource requests based on initial estimates rather than actual usage data.
    This led to significant over-provisioning — nodes were running at low utilization while
    costs continued to climb.
  </p>

  <h2>Implementation Details</h2>

  <h3>1. Metrics Collection & Analysis</h3>
  <p>Established a baseline by collecting 2-4 weeks of resource usage data from Datadog:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Captured P95 and P99 CPU and memory usage per microservice</li>
    <li>Identified services with less than 20% resource utilization</li>
    <li>Mapped peak usage patterns against request/limit configurations</li>
    <li>Flagged services with memory limits far exceeding actual heap usage</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>2. Right-Sizing Resource Requests</h3>
  <p>Adjusted Kubernetes resource requests based on actual consumption:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Set CPU requests to P95 usage + 20% buffer</li>
    <li>Set memory requests to P99 usage + 15% headroom</li>
    <li>Removed artificially high limits that prevented efficient bin-packing</li>
    <li>Updated Helm chart values across all microservice repositories</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>3. HPA Reconfiguration</h3>
  <p>Tuned autoscaling to work with the new resource profiles:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Adjusted HPA target utilization thresholds</li>
    <li>Configured appropriate min/max replica counts per service tier</li>
    <li>Validated scaling behavior under load testing</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Architecture Diagram</h2>
  <MermaidDiagram diagram={diagrams["toast-io"]} />

  <h2>Results</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>40-60% reduction</strong> in EKS compute costs</li>
    <li>Significant decrease in node count through better bin-packing</li>
    <li>Improved pod scheduling efficiency — fewer pending pods</li>
    <li>Zero performance regressions across all 120+ services</li>
    <li>Established a repeatable right-sizing review process for future services</li>
  </ul>
</ProjectLayout>
